---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = "15-Year vs 30-Year Mortgage Payment (Trade-offs)";
const description =
  "Compare 15-year and 30-year mortgages as different required payment lifestyles, not just different interest totals. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-22";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/guides/mortgage-payment-15-vs-30-year"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview, TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview]}
  robots="noindex, follow"
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">15 vs 30 year</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>15-year vs 30-year mortgage payment</h1>
    <p>
      This page is for the buyer whose real decision is not just total interest, but whether they want a faster payoff built into the
      required payment or flexibility preserved inside the required payment.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/amortization-schedule-calculator">Amortization schedule</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-total-cost-vs-payment">Payment vs total cost</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    reviewScope="Term-choice review, required-payment framing, and routing between total-cost comparison, affordability, and payment flexibility."
    reviewedOn={lastUpdated}
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when term choice is the real mortgage-payment decision</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when the home and rate family are already acceptable, but the required pace of repayment is still undecided.</li>
      <li>If your broader question is monthly payment versus total borrowing cost, move next to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-total-cost-vs-payment">mortgage payment vs total cost</a>.</li>
      <li>If the real blocker is budget fragility, move to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">mortgage payment affordability checklist</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">The real difference is behavioral, not just mathematical</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      A 15-year loan is forced payoff versus optional prepayment. It builds discipline into the required payment. A 30-year loan
      preserves a lower minimum, which can be useful, but only if you treat that flexibility intentionally.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">What a 15-year really buys</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li>Faster equity growth and lower total interest.</li>
        <li>Less freedom to slow down during expensive months.</li>
        <li>A payment shape that forces consistency.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">What a 30-year really buys</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li>Lower required payment and more breathing room.</li>
        <li>More dependence on self-discipline if you plan to prepay anyway.</li>
        <li>A payment profile that can absorb uncertainty better.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Flexibility only helps if it is protected</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      A 30-year flexibility only matters if you protect the cash-flow gap instead of letting it disappear into routine spending. That
      is why the comparison is partly a household-management decision, not just a mortgage calculation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Run the comparison like two lifestyles</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      The same house can produce two very different required lifestyles. One version demands a higher fixed payment every month. The
      other asks whether you value optionality more than a built-in faster payoff.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">When to move to a different page</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>If the broader issue is total dollars paid, move to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-total-cost-vs-payment">mortgage payment total cost vs payment</a>.</li>
      <li>If you want to model extra payments instead of changing term, move to <a href="/guides/extra-mortgage-payments">extra mortgage payments</a>.</li>
      <li>If the real question is whether the higher payment is too aggressive, move to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">mortgage payment affordability checklist</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/explore/home-loan-toolkit/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Your home loan toolkit
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/ready-to-buy-a-home/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Ready to buy a home?
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Compare payments</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-total-cost-vs-payment">Compare total cost</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Check affordability</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-22</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
